WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.200
Video two. Install Hisaab on Windows, and
start it the first time.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:11.884
You need a PC with Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit,
and about 400 MB of free disk space.

00:00:12.084 --> 00:00:17.501
The install has five steps: download, keep,
run, setup, and the first start.

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:24.352
Open the Hisaab releases page. Under Assets,
find the file Hisaab_…_x64-setup.exe.

00:00:24.382 --> 00:00:28.598
Click it. The other files are for the updates
and the Microsoft Store.

00:00:29.678 --> 00:00:35.696
The browser can ask: make sure you trust this file. The
file is new, so the browser does not know it yet.

00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:40.744
Click the small arrow next to Delete, then
click Keep anyway. Then open the file.

00:00:42.276 --> 00:00:46.359
Now Windows can show a blue box: Windows
protected your PC.

00:00:46.389 --> 00:00:48.339
Click More info.

00:00:48.569 --> 00:00:55.385
Check the line App: it shows the Hisaab setup file. Windows shows
this box because the file has no paid signature yet.

00:00:55.569 --> 00:00:58.853
Click Run anyway. You do this one time only.

00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:05.817
The Hisaab setup opens. It installs Hisaab for you
only, so it needs no administrator password.

00:01:05.847 --> 00:01:10.198
Click Next, then Next again. At the end,
Hisaab starts.

00:01:11.278 --> 00:01:16.162
The first start can take up to one minute.
Windows checks the new program one time.

00:01:16.192 --> 00:01:21.143
Then Hisaab asks where your books go. For a
new start, take the empty data folder.

00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:24.409
To look around first, open the demo company.

00:01:25.642 --> 00:01:32.193
Your books stay on this PC, in
Documents\Hisaab\Data. Each company has its own folder.

00:01:32.123 --> 00:01:38.405
From the first day, Hisaab takes a daily backup of
every company, in Documents\Hisaab\backups.

00:01:38.606 --> 00:01:44.225
Updates come by themselves. At each start, Hisaab
checks for a new version, and tells you.

00:01:44.155 --> 00:01:50.572
Press F1, then Upgrade. Hisaab backs up every company
first, installs the update, and starts again.

00:01:50.872 --> 00:01:53.623
Upgrade is in the F1 Help menu.

00:01:54.272 --> 00:01:58.690
After the update, the Gateway shows the backup
that Hisaab took before it.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:03.655
Hisaab is ready. Next, bring your company from
Tally in one step.

